{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1155453-dtf-earthbound-phylacteries","id":1155453,"title":"DtF Earthbound Phylacteries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-03T11:10:43-07:00","id":1155453,"title":"DtF Earthbound Phylacteries","content":"Why do the Earthbound have objects that they inhabit vs People like the current Demons returning from Hell? <br /> How would an &quot;elder&quot; Demon in a human form be created?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13458-adamg","name":"AdamG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T15:13:44-07:00","id":1155559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1155453-dtf-earthbound-phylacteries#post1155453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do the Earthbound have objects that they inhabit vs People like the current Demons returning from Hell?<br /> How would an &quot;elder&quot; Demon in a human form be created?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because torment 10 causes any human host they inhabit to die painfully.<br /> <br /> Just like normal demons with a larger spread of lores. They'd also start with faith 6+ because of the faith requirement for the vessel when summoning a lord of hell. Honestly I don't see why the earthbound would Want to inhabit humans when just enchanting a human-sized doll or statue with the ability to move would give them all the benefits of an urges/mastery rating, the indestructibility of a phylactery, and the ability to move around the real work in mortal guise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T10:47:20-07:00","id":1155790,"title":"","content":"Actually just to differentiate them from current Demons, since most of the rules contradict themselves.<br /> <br /> For the actual mechanical explanation, it is said that the potency of the Earthbound is so great they burn down human vessels. Their supplement even have the rules to inhabit humans for a time and the effects on the vessel.<br /> <br /> But the game at no point presumes that current Demons have to follow such rules, even after they become Earthbound themselves for a time.<br /> <br /> The lore also states that the old Earthbound are beings of greater power, while the current rupture in Hell's walls only let little Demons out.<br /> <br /> It is contradicted again by the rules simply not creating absolutely no power for the Earthbound that isn't available to other Demons with experience.<br /> <br /> Since I like the similarity between Demons and Earthbound more than the distinction, I usually just consider the Earthbound to fucked-up in their minds to even try to inhabit human vessels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d",